ires a separate, fully executed Commercial Licensing and Royalty Agreement with the Licensor.  * Licensing Fees: Licensee shall pay the required upfront deployment and node-issuance fees.  * Royalty Payments: Licensee shall remit periodic, percentage-based royalties derived from gross revenues, subscription models, or network operational utility utilizing the Software.  * Reporting: Detailed usage logs, telemetry metrics, and financial accounts shall be provided to the Licensor on a strict quarterly basis.  5. NETWORK TELEMETRY, DATA ACCESS & MONITORING By connecting, configuring, or operating any node utilizing the Software, the Licensee explicitly consents to continuous network telemetry monitoring. The Licensor reserves the right to track operational data, node health, connection metadata, and usage metrics automatically to verify compliance and compute accurate royalty obligations.  6. REMOTE REVOCATION & NODE TERMINATION The Licensor retains the unilateral right to instantly revoke cryptographic certificates, blacklist public keys, or terminate network synchronization for any node suspected of breaching this Agreement, bypassing telemetry, or operating outside the scope of an executed commercial license.  7. AUDIT AND COMPLIANCE The Licensor reserves the right, upon reasonable notice, to audit network telemetry, operational logs, and financial records to verify compliance with deployment terms and ensure accurate calculation of owed royalties.  8. INDEMNIFICATION Licensee agrees to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the Licensor from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, or expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or in any way connected with the Licensee's deployment, modification, or commercial operation of the Software.  9. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with applicable commercial and intellectual property laws, without regard to conflict of law principles. Any