uest Metrics (Firebase Hosting) * **CDN Edge Logging:** By linking Firebase Hosting to Cloud Logging, you get detailed logs for every single web asset request.  * **Key Metrics:** You can track **Request Latency**, **Cache Hits vs. Misses**, and CDN performance to optimize your frontend loading times.  ### 3. Server-Side Rendering (SSR) Logs (Firebase App Hosting) If you are migrating or building a modern framework app (like Next.js or Angular) using App Hosting: * **Separated Logs:** Static build logs (from Cloud Build) and active server-side runtime logs (from Cloud Run) are automatically captured and separated, making it simple to diagnose build failures versus runtime crashes.  ### 4. App Check Verification & Audit Logs To protect your Web app's backend APIs from abuse: * **Verification Insights:** App Check generates audit logs of all requests hitting your database or backend. You can analyze these logs to see exactly how many requests are verified, outdated, or fraudulent before deciding to enforce blocking rules.  ### 5. Cost-Saving Exclusion Filters Since your project is on the **Spark plan**: * **Exclude to Save:** You can set up custom log filters to discard high-volume, low-importance logs (such as success statuses) so you stay safely within the free logging tiers and avoid unexpected usage hikes.","response":"[LEXICON: AI] Artificial intelligence: software that performs tasks associated with learning, reasoning, language, or decision support.","hash":"c9621a041902d706a8d973d4f08e86df863277c671fd1fbaced5c3083b379968","sessionId":"WS-66BF1D"}|1788504002067
98933f71b2d53d1f34aa94f8d06dea213569f9d13f51b2f9e6da5fca5a4c1f96 631e565699b6df3c25ee29461605872119cd56db740a0edf9d79e40e78dd9a3d|{"type":"chat","text":"#!/bin/bash  # Colors for readability RED='\\033[0;31m' GREEN='\\033[0;32m' YELLOW='\\033[0;33m' NC='\\033[0m' # No Color  echo \"=== ${GREEN}ZTPK SYSTEM STATUS CHECK${NC} ===\"  # Check HashBasket Bridge HASHBASKET_PID=$(pgrep -f \"node.*hashbasket-bridge.js\") if [ -z \"$HASHBASKET_PID\" ]; then     echo \"[${RED}FAIL${NC}] HashBasket Bridge: Not running\" else     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] HashBasket Bridge: Running (PID: $HASHBASKET_PID)\" fi  # Check GEM Listener GEM_PID=$(pgrep -f \"python.*gem_listener.py\") if [ -z \"$GEM_PID\" ]; then     echo \"[${RED}FAIL${NC}] GEM Listener: Not running\" else     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] GEM Listener: Running (PID: $GEM_PID)\"     # Check GEM socket     if [ -S \"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/ztpk/gem_trigger.sock\" ]; then         echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] GEM Socket: Active\"     else         echo \"[${RED}FAIL${NC}] GEM Socket: Not found\"     fi fi  # Check Dead Man’s Switch DMS_PID=$(pgrep -f \"python.*dead_mans_switch.py\") if [ -z \"$DMS_PID\" ]; then     echo \"[${YELLOW}WARN${NC}] Dead Man’s Switch: Not running (expected if not testing interdiction)\" else     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] Dead Man’s Switch: Running (PID: $DMS_PID)\" fi  # Check Rogue AP Monitor ROGUE_PID=$(pgrep -f \"python.*rogue_ap_monitor.py\") if [ -z \"$ROGUE_PID\" ]; then     echo \"[${YELLOW}WARN${NC}] Rogue AP Monitor: Not running (WiFi may be down)\" else     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] Rogue AP Monitor: Running (PID: $ROGUE_PID)\" fi  # Check WebSocket Port if nc -z localhost 8080; then     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] WebSocket Port (8080): Open\" else     echo \"[${RED}FAIL${NC}] WebSocket Port (8080): Closed\" fi  # Check Stratum Port if nc -z localhost 3333; then     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] Stratum Port (3333): Open\" else     echo \"[${RED}FAIL${NC}] Stratum Port (3333): Closed\" fi  # Check Logs if [ -f \"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/ztpk/rogue_aps.json\" ]; then     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] Rogue AP Logs: Found\" else     echo \"[${YELLOW}WARN${NC}] Rogue AP Logs: Not found (no detections yet?)\" fi  if [ -f \"/data/data/com.termux/files/home/ztpk/blacklist.txt\" ]; then     echo \"[${GREEN}OK${NC}] Blacklist: Found\" else     echo \"[${YELLOW}WARN${NC}] Blacklist: Not found (no blacklisted IPs yet?)\" fi  echo \"=== ${GREEN}STATUS CHECK COMPLETE${NC} ===\"","sender":"DEV-FBB3AEA5","transport":"websocket"}|1788504006315
